.docname {Accessibility}
.include {docs}

gol-bevy can be used from the keyboard alone, and exposes its interface to screen readers and other assistive tools through [AccessKit](https://accesskit.dev).

## Keyboard navigation

- .keybinding {Tab} moves between the visible, enabled controls; .keybinding {Shift+Tab} moves back.
- .keybinding {Enter} or .keybinding {Space} activates the focused button.
- Click the board, or press .keybinding {Esc} in a text field or the slider, to give the keyboard back to the board shortcuts.

Focused controls have a bright outline, and are scrolled into view if the palette or a dialog has to scroll. Hidden controls, such as those in a hidden palette, are left out of the tab order.

While a text field or the speed slider has focus, board shortcuts are disabled, so typing a pattern name does not run or clear the board.

## Colours

The **High contrast** theme in [Settings](settings.qd#theme) uses black panels, white text, bright green cells, and a yellow focus outline. A **Light** theme is available too. Every theme keeps text at a contrast of at least 4.5:1 against its background, and live cells and the pointer outline at least 3:1 against empty cells.

## Dialogs

Dialogs are modal: .keybinding {Tab} stays inside the open dialog. The Help and Diagnostics dialogs focus their **Close** button when they open.

.keybinding {Esc} closes a dialog, and focus returns to the control that opened it. The key that opened Help (.keybinding {/}) or Diagnostics (.keybinding {F3}) closes it again.

## Screen readers

- Buttons expose their action and, for toggles such as tools, patterns, **Grid**, and **Palette**, whether they are selected.
- **Play** is announced as *Play* or *Pause*, and **Edges** with the current mode.
- Text fields expose their name and value.
- The speed slider exposes its value and supports increment and decrement actions.
- Validation messages, such as a rejected board size or an import error, are announced politely when they appear.

## Text editing

Text fields support the platform clipboard shortcuts (.keybinding {Mod+C}, .keybinding {Mod+X}, .keybinding {Mod+V}, and .keybinding {Mod+A}) and selection with .keybinding {Shift} and the arrow keys.
